ou to  specific types of data that could be  that could be acquired from next  generation sequencing so genomics  transcriptomics and metagenomics and  talk a little bit about maybe things  that you haven't thought of how  bioinformatics is actually used to study  precision medicine or astronaut health  in space  now also a big component of  bioinformatics as i mentioned is the  application of data analysis techniques  and tools to large data sets and coding  is a critical component so as you've  seen one of the critical elements is to  understand how and why and then have the  practical skills and so the second  option that was mentioned in the  beginning so the first one was genomics  in the virtual lab the second one was  coding or biomedical data analysis in r  and python so in this course you will  already get an introduction to  coding in r which is a popular  method of analyzing different types of  biological data where you will have  access to different examples of just  getting to know what coding is why do we  need coding and how to read  use  to load the data things like that so  that's going to be very useful because  one of the practical examples here is  the ability to actually  run code and practice fixing the code  that is given to you without having to  you know  take too much time of  yours  to actually learn everything from  scratch so we're not going to learn  things like hello world we're going to  jump into how to load data and this data  is going to be biological data or the  type of data that you are expected to  use in the domain of bioinformatics and  once we get into this you will see that  you will start to appreciate syntax you  will know how to load and produce  simple plots that are informative you  will  interpret these plots and then as it  becomes more and more complex so here  you will find assignments  those will introduce you to more and  more complex methods of analysis  including analysis of complex data  analysis using complex methods like  machine learning and deep learning and  also ability to integrate multiple  sources of information to actually  answer real research questions  so along the way as you go through this  course work you will realize that a lot  of this course work is sourced from  experts in the field  and experts in the field are people that  have a long history of  maybe doing research or using such  skills in the domain of biotechnology  and pharma  and getting to know these people you  will realize that they all have a rich  history and a path of how they got to  where they are today so  to briefly introduce some of these  people  i want to  highlight a couple examples  and those examples are going to  demonstrate kind of the quality of the  people that you will be  exposed  [Music]

